/-!
# Bundles over `X × ℂP¹` are clutchings; the clutched lines `L m`

Let `X` be compact Hausdorff and `F` a finite-rank core over `X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)`, and let `E` be
its restriction to `X × {[1 : 1]}`, that is its pullback along `x ↦ (x, [1 : 1])`. Then `F` is
isomorphic to the clutching `E.clutching f` of `E` by some automorphism `f` of the pullback of `E`
to `X × Circle` (`TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.exists_iso_clutching`), and over `ℂ` the
automorphism may be taken a Laurent polynomial in the circle coordinate
(`TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.exists_iso_clutching_laurent`). These are the first steps of the
product theorem of [Hatcher2017, §2.1].

The file also treats the clutched lines `L m = (trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X m)`,
clutched by `u ↦ u ^ m`, for `X` paracompact and R₁: `L m ⊕ L n ≅ L (m + n) ⊕ L 0`, hence in
`K(X × ℂP¹)` the class of `L m` is `1 + m • (1 - [H])`, with `H = L (-1)` the pullback of the
tautological line, and in particular `[H⁻¹] = [L 1] = 2 - [H]`.

## Main definitions and results

* `TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.nonempty_pullback_affineChartMap_iso`: over `X × (Fin 1 → ℂ)`,
  the pullback of `F` along the inverse `ProjectiveLine.affineChartMap X i` of an affine chart of
  the projective line is the pullback of `E` along the projection, since the affine line
  contracts to the coordinate `1` of `[1 : 1]`
  (`TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.nonempty_iso_pullback_fst`). Here `E` is the pullback of `F`
  along `ProjectiveLine.prodMkOne X`.
* `TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.nonempty_pullback_subtypeVal_iso_of_subset_affineOpen`: hence the
  same holds for the restriction of `F` to `X × S`, for any set `S` inside an affine open.
* `TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.exists_iso_clutching`: every core over `X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)` is a
  clutching of its restriction to `X × {[1 : 1]}`.
* `TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.exists_iso_clutching_laurent`: for a complex core, the clutching
  function may be taken a Laurent family `laurentHom N a`, with fibre map
  `∑_{|i| ≤ N} u ^ i • (a i).fiberMap x` at `(x, u)`.
* `TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.whitneySum_clutching_circleZPowIso`: `L m ⊕ L n ≅ L (m + n) ⊕ L 0`.
* `TauCeti.SplitK0.of_clutching_circleZPowIso`: the class of `L m` is `1 + m • (1 - [H])`;
  `of_clutching_circleZPowIso_zero` and `of_clutching_circleZPowIso_neg_one` are the cases
  `m = 0` and `m = -1`, which need no hypothesis on `X`.
* `TauCeti.SplitK0.of_clutching_circleZPowIso_one`: `[H⁻¹] = 2 - [H]`.
* `TauCeti.SplitK0.of_clutching_circleZPowIso_mem_closure`: the class of every `L m` lies in the
  additive subgroup generated by `1` and `[H]`.

The discs, the annulus and the maps between products with them that the proof uses, such as
`ProjectiveLine.circleToAnnulus` and the radial deformation `ProjectiveLine.annulusDeformation`,
are in `SymplecticGeometry.Topology.ComplexProjectiveSpace.ProjectiveLine`.

## Proof

Each of the two discs lies in an affine open, so the restriction of `F` to its product with `X` is
the pullback of `E` along the projection, by homotopy invariance of pullbacks applied to the
segments to `[1 : 1]` in the affine chart
(`TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.nonempty_iso_pullback_fst`). By
`TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.isoGlue`, `F` is then the gluing of the pullback of `E` by the
transition `g` of the two isomorphisms over the product of `X` with the annulus. Let `f` be `g`
restricted to `X × Circle`. The radial deformation of the annulus onto the circle joins `g` to
`clutchingAut E f`, which glues to `E.clutching f`, and gluings by homotopic automorphisms are
isomorphic (`TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.nonempty_iso_glue_of_homotopic`).

For a complex core, `TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.exists_iso_clutching_laurentHom` then replaces
`f` by a Laurent family whose clutching is isomorphic to that by `f`.

For the lines, `L m ⊕ L n` and `L (m + n) ⊕ L 0` are the clutchings of the sum of two trivial
lines by `diag (u ^ m, u ^ n)` and `diag (u ^ (m + n), 1)`
(`TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.clutching_whitneySum`). These are joined in `GL₂(ℂ)` by
`diag (u ^ m, 1) · R_t · diag (1, u ^ n) · R_t⁻¹`, with `R_t` the rotation by `π t / 2`, which
swaps the two coordinates at `t = 1`; so the clutchings are isomorphic
(`TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.nonempty_iso_clutching_of_homotopic`). Taking `n = 1` and
`n = -1` gives the class of `L m` by induction on `m`, from `L 0 ≅ 1`
(`TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.clutching_one`) and `L (-1) ≅ H`
(`TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore.clutching_z`).

## References

* [A. Hatcher, *Vector Bundles and K-Theory*][Hatcher2017], §2.1 (every bundle over `X × S²` is a
  clutching; the relation `[H⁻¹] = 2 - [H]` and the rotation that proves it).
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Set CategoryTheory Projectivization

open scoped LinearAlgebra.Projectivization

namespace TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore

open SymplecticGeometry.ProjectiveLine

variable {𝕜 X : Type*} [NontriviallyNormedField 𝕜] [TopologicalSpace X]
  [CompactSpace X] [T2Space X] [NormedAlgebra ℝ 𝕜] [CompleteSpace 𝕜]
  (F : FiniteRankBundleCore 𝕜 (X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)))

/-! ### The restriction of a core to the product with a disc -/

/-- **A core is trivial along the affine line.** For `X` compact Hausdorff and a core `F` over
`X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)`, the pullback of `F` along the inverse of an affine chart in the second
factor is isomorphic to the pullback along the projection `X × (Fin 1 → ℂ) → X` of the restriction
of `F` to `X × {[1 : 1]}`. -/
theorem nonempty_pullback_affineChartMap_iso (i : Fin 2) :
    Nonempty (F.pullback (affineChartMap X i) ≅
      (F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).pullback ContinuousMap.fst) := by
  -- The affine line contracts to the coordinate `1` of `[1 : 1]`.
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := (F.pullback (affineChartMap X i)).nonempty_iso_pullback_fst (1 : Fin 1 → ℂ)
  have hk : (affineChartMap X i).comp ((ContinuousMap.id X).prodMk (.const X 1)) =
      prodMkOne X :=
    ContinuousMap.ext fun x ↦ by simp
  rw [pullback_comp F, hk] at e
  exact ⟨e⟩

/-- **A core is trivial over the product with a part of an affine open.** For `X` compact
Hausdorff, a core `F` over `X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)` and a set `S` inside the affine open `i` of the
projective line, the restriction of `F` to `X × S` is isomorphic to that of the pullback along the
projection of the restriction of `F` to `X × {[1 : 1]}`. -/
theorem nonempty_pullback_subtypeVal_iso_of_subset_affineOpen {i : Fin 2}
    {S : Set (ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ))} (hS : S ⊆ affineOpen i) :
    Nonempty (F.pullback (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal (Prod.snd ⁻¹' S)) ≅
      ((F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).pullback ContinuousMap.fst).pullback
        (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal (Prod.snd ⁻¹' S))) := by
  -- The coordinates of `X × S` in `X × (Fin 1 → ℂ)`.
  let k : C(↥(Prod.snd ⁻¹' S : Set (X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ))), X × (Fin 1 → ℂ)) :=
    ⟨fun w ↦ (w.val.1, affineChart i w.val.2),
      (continuous_fst.comp continuous_subtypeVal).prodMk
        (continuousOn_iff_continuous_domRestrict.1 ((continuousOn_affineChart i).mono hS) |>.comp
          ((continuous_snd.comp continuous_subtypeVal).subtype_mk fun w ↦ w.property))⟩
  have hk : (affineChartMap X i).comp k = ContinuousMap.subtypeVal (Prod.snd ⁻¹' S) :=
    ContinuousMap.ext fun w ↦ Prod.ext (by simp [affineChartMap_apply, k])
      (by simpa [affineChartMap_apply, k] using
        (affineChart i).left_inv (by rw [affineChart_source]; exact hS w.property))
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := F.nonempty_pullback_affineChartMap_iso i
  refine ⟨eqToIso ?_ ≪≫ (pullbackFunctor k).mapIso e ≪≫ eqToIso ?_⟩
  · rw [pullbackFunctor_obj, pullback_comp, hk]
  · rw [pullbackFunctor_obj, pullback_comp, pullback_comp, pullback_comp]
    exact congrArg F.pullback (ContinuousMap.ext fun _ ↦ rfl)

/-! ### Every core over `X × ℂP¹` is a clutching -/

/-- **Every bundle over `X × ℂP¹` is a clutching.** Let `X` be compact Hausdorff and `F` a
finite-rank core over `X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)`, and let `E` be its restriction to `X × {[1 : 1]}`,
the pullback of `F` along `x ↦ (x, [1 : 1])`. Then `F` is isomorphic to the clutching of `E` by
some automorphism `f` of the pullback of `E` to `X × Circle`. -/
theorem exists_iso_clutching :
    ∃ f : (F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).pullback (ContinuousMap.fst : C(X × Circle, X)) ≅
        (F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).pullback (ContinuousMap.fst : C(X × Circle, X)),
      Nonempty (F ≅ (F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).clutching f) := by
  obtain ⟨φ⟩ := F.nonempty_pullback_subtypeVal_iso_of_subset_affineOpen
    (S := innerDisc) innerDisc_subset_affineOpen
  obtain ⟨ψ⟩ := F.nonempty_pullback_subtypeVal_iso_of_subset_affineOpen
    (S := outerDisc) outerDisc_subset_affineOpen
  have hU : IsOpen (Prod.snd ⁻¹' innerDisc : Set (X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ))) :=
    isOpen_innerDisc.preimage continuous_snd
  have hV : IsOpen (Prod.snd ⁻¹' outerDisc : Set (X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ))) :=
    isOpen_outerDisc.preimage continuous_snd
  have hUV : (Prod.snd ⁻¹' innerDisc ∪ Prod.snd ⁻¹' outerDisc : Set (X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ))) =
      univ := by
    rw [← preimage_union, innerDisc_union_outerDisc, preimage_univ]
  -- The pullbacks of `E` along the restrictions of the projection to `X × Circle`, through
  -- `circleToAnnulus`, and to the annulus part of `(X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)) × I`, through
  -- `annulusDeformation`, are its pullbacks along the projections.
  have hc : (((F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).pullback ContinuousMap.fst).pullback
      (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal (Prod.snd ⁻¹' innerDisc ∩ Prod.snd ⁻¹' outerDisc))).pullback
        (circleToAnnulus X) = (F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).pullback ContinuousMap.fst := by
    simp [pullback_comp]
  have hd : (((F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).pullback ContinuousMap.fst).pullback
      (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal (Prod.snd ⁻¹' innerDisc ∩ Prod.snd ⁻¹' outerDisc))).pullback
        (annulusDeformation X) =
      (((F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).pullback ContinuousMap.fst).pullback
        (ContinuousMap.fst : C((X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)) × unitInterval, X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)))).pullback
        (ContinuousMap.subtypeVal (Prod.fst ⁻¹' (Prod.snd ⁻¹' innerDisc) ∩
          Prod.fst ⁻¹' (Prod.snd ⁻¹' outerDisc))) := by
    simp [pullback_comp]
  -- The casts `eqToHom` have the identity as fibre maps.
  have hc' : ∀ (y : X × Circle) (v : Fin (F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).rank → 𝕜),
      (eqToHom hc.symm).fiberMap y v = v := fun _ _ ↦ funext fun _ ↦ by simp [Fin.cast_eq_self]
  have hd' : ∀ y (v : Fin (F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).rank → 𝕜),
      (eqToHom hd.symm).fiberMap y v = v := fun _ _ ↦ funext fun _ ↦ by simp [Fin.cast_eq_self]
  -- The clutching function: the transition of `φ` and `ψ` on `X × Circle`.
  let f := eqToIso hc.symm ≪≫ (pullbackFunctor (circleToAnnulus X)).mapIso (glueTransition φ ψ) ≪≫
    eqToIso hc
  refine ⟨f, ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_iso_glue_of_homotopic _ hU hV hUV
    (g₀ := glueTransition φ ψ) (g₁ := clutchingAut (F.pullback (prodMkOne X)) f)
    (eqToIso hd.symm ≪≫ (pullbackFunctor (annulusDeformation X)).mapIso (glueTransition φ ψ) ≪≫
      eqToIso hd)
    (fun w ↦ by
      ext v i
      simp [hd', annulusDeformation_zero, Fin.cast_eq_self])
    (fun w ↦ by
      ext v i
      simp [f, hc', hd', annulusDeformation_one, Fin.cast_eq_self])
  exact ⟨isoGlue φ ψ hU hV hUV ≪≫ e⟩

/-- **Every bundle over `X × ℂP¹` is a clutching by a Laurent clutching function.** Let `X` be
compact Hausdorff and `F` a finite-rank complex core over `X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)`, and let `E` be its
restriction to `X × {[1 : 1]}`. Then there are `N : ℕ`, endomorphisms `a i` of `E` and an
automorphism `g` of the pullback of `E` to `X × Circle` whose underlying morphism is the Laurent
family `laurentHom N a`, with fibre map `∑_{|i| ≤ N} u ^ i • (a i).fiberMap x` at `(x, u)`, such
that `F` is isomorphic to the clutching of `E` by `g`. -/
theorem exists_iso_clutching_laurent (F : FiniteRankBundleCore ℂ (X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ))) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (a : ℤ → (F.pullback (prodMkOne X) ⟶ F.pullback (prodMkOne X)))
      (g : (F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).pullback (ContinuousMap.fst : C(X × Circle, X)) ≅
        (F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).pullback (ContinuousMap.fst : C(X × Circle, X))),
      g.hom = laurentHom N a ∧ Nonempty (F ≅ (F.pullback (prodMkOne X)).clutching g) := by
  obtain ⟨f, ⟨e⟩⟩ := F.exists_iso_clutching
  obtain ⟨N, a, g, hg, ⟨e'⟩⟩ := exists_iso_clutching_laurentHom f
  exact ⟨N, a, g, hg, ⟨e ≪≫ e'⟩⟩

end TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore

/-! ### Hatcher's rotation in `GL₂(ℂ)` -/

namespace SymplecticGeometry.ProductSphere

open TauCeti

open scoped unitInterval

/-- The plane `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` in the block coordinates of the Whitney sum of two lines. -/
local notation "V" => (Fin 1 → ℂ) × (Fin 1 → ℂ)

/-- The rotation of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ` by the angle `θ`, as a unit of its operators: `(v, w)` goes to
`(cos θ • v - sin θ • w, sin θ • v + cos θ • w)`. -/
private def rotUnit (θ : ℂ) : (V →L[ℂ] V)ˣ where
  val := Complex.cos θ • 1 + Complex.sin θ •
    (-(ContinuousLinearMap.snd ℂ (Fin 1 → ℂ) (Fin 1 → ℂ))).prod (ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℂ _ _)
  inv := Complex.cos θ • 1 - Complex.sin θ •
    (-(ContinuousLinearMap.snd ℂ (Fin 1 → ℂ) (Fin 1 → ℂ))).prod (ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℂ _ _)
  val_inv := by
    ext v i <;>
      simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.inl_apply,
        ContinuousLinearMap.inr_apply, mul_apply_eq_comp, sub_apply, add_apply, smul_apply,
        one_apply_eq_self, Prod.smul_mk, smul_zero, ContinuousLinearMap.prod_apply, neg_apply,
        ContinuousLinearMap.coe_snd', ContinuousLinearMap.coe_fst', neg_zero, Prod.mk_sub_mk,
        Prod.mk_add_mk, sub_zero, zero_sub, zero_add, smul_neg, neg_neg, sub_neg_eq_add,
        Pi.add_apply, Pi.neg_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, Pi.zero_apply] <;>
      first | ring1 | linear_combination (v i) * Complex.cos_sq_add_sin_sq θ
  inv_val := by
    ext v i <;>
      simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.inl_apply,
        ContinuousLinearMap.inr_apply, mul_apply_eq_comp, sub_apply, add_apply, smul_apply,
        one_apply_eq_self, Prod.smul_mk, smul_zero, ContinuousLinearMap.prod_apply, neg_apply,
        ContinuousLinearMap.coe_snd', ContinuousLinearMap.coe_fst', neg_zero, Prod.mk_sub_mk,
        Prod.mk_add_mk, zero_add, add_zero, smul_neg, sub_neg_eq_add,
        Pi.add_apply, Pi.sub_apply, Pi.neg_apply, Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, Pi.zero_apply] <;>
      first | ring1 | linear_combination (v i) * Complex.cos_sq_add_sin_sq θ

/-- The diagonal operator `(v, w) ↦ (a • v, b • w)` of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ`, as a unit. -/
private def diagUnit (a b : ℂˣ) : (V →L[ℂ] V)ˣ where
  val := ((a : ℂ) • ContinuousLinearMap.id ℂ _).prodMap ((b : ℂ) • ContinuousLinearMap.id ℂ _)
  inv := (((a⁻¹ : ℂˣ) : ℂ) • ContinuousLinearMap.id ℂ _).prodMap
    (((b⁻¹ : ℂˣ) : ℂ) • ContinuousLinearMap.id ℂ _)
  val_inv := by ext v i <;> simp
  inv_val := by ext v i <;> simp

/-- Hatcher's homotopy from `diag (u ^ m, u ^ n)` to `diag (u ^ (m + n), 1)` in `GL₂(ℂ)`: at time
`t`, the product `diag (u ^ m, 1) · R · diag (1, u ^ n) · R⁻¹`, with `R` the rotation by
`π t / 2`. -/
private def rotationHomotopy (m n : ℤ) (t : I) (u : Circle) : (V →L[ℂ] V)ˣ :=
  diagUnit (Circle.toUnits (u ^ m)) 1 * rotUnit (Real.pi / 2 * (t : ℝ)) *
    diagUnit 1 (Circle.toUnits (u ^ n)) * (rotUnit (Real.pi / 2 * (t : ℝ)))⁻¹

private theorem continuous_rotationHomotopy (m n : ℤ) :
    Continuous fun p : I × Circle ↦ (rotationHomotopy m n p.1 p.2 : V →L[ℂ] V) := by
  have hθ : Continuous fun p : I × Circle ↦ (Real.pi / 2 * ((p.1 : ℝ) : ℂ)) := by fun_prop
  have hc : Continuous fun p : I × Circle ↦ Complex.cos (Real.pi / 2 * ((p.1 : ℝ) : ℂ)) :=
    Complex.continuous_cos.comp hθ
  have hs : Continuous fun p : I × Circle ↦ Complex.sin (Real.pi / 2 * ((p.1 : ℝ) : ℂ)) :=
    Complex.continuous_sin.comp hθ
  have hu (k : ℤ) : Continuous fun p : I × Circle ↦ ((p.2 ^ k : Circle) : ℂ) := by fun_prop
  have hd₁ : Continuous fun p : I × Circle ↦
      (diagUnit (Circle.toUnits (p.2 ^ m)) 1 : V →L[ℂ] V) :=
    ((hu m).smul continuous_const).prod_mapL ℂ continuous_const
  have hd₂ : Continuous fun p : I × Circle ↦
      (diagUnit 1 (Circle.toUnits (p.2 ^ n)) : V →L[ℂ] V) :=
    continuous_const.prod_mapL ℂ ((hu n).smul continuous_const)
  have hr : Continuous fun p : I × Circle ↦
      (rotUnit (Real.pi / 2 * ((p.1 : ℝ) : ℂ)) : V →L[ℂ] V) :=
    (hc.smul continuous_const).add (hs.smul continuous_const)
  have hr' : Continuous fun p : I × Circle ↦
      (((rotUnit (Real.pi / 2 * ((p.1 : ℝ) : ℂ)))⁻¹ : (V →L[ℂ] V)ˣ) : V →L[ℂ] V) :=
    (hc.smul continuous_const).sub (hs.smul continuous_const)
  simp only [rotationHomotopy, Units.val_mul]
  exact ((hd₁.mul hr).mul hd₂).mul hr'

private theorem rotationHomotopy_zero (m n : ℤ) (u : Circle) :
    (rotationHomotopy m n 0 u : V →L[ℂ] V) = ((u : ℂ) ^ m • ContinuousLinearMap.id ℂ _).prodMap
      ((u : ℂ) ^ n • ContinuousLinearMap.id ℂ _) := by
  ext v i <;> simp [rotationHomotopy, rotUnit, diagUnit]

private theorem rotationHomotopy_one (m n : ℤ) (u : Circle) :
    (rotationHomotopy m n 1 u : V →L[ℂ] V) =
      ((u : ℂ) ^ (m + n) • ContinuousLinearMap.id ℂ _).prodMap
        ((u : ℂ) ^ (0 : ℤ) • ContinuousLinearMap.id ℂ _) := by
  ext v i <;> simp [rotationHomotopy, rotUnit, diagUnit, zpow_add₀ (Circle.coe_ne_zero u)]
  ring

/-- A unit of the operators of `ℂ ⊕ ℂ`, read in the coordinates `Fin (1 + 1) → ℂ` through
`splitCoords`, is the block map that its operator gives. -/
private theorem splitCoords_conj_unitsEquiv (u : (V →L[ℂ] V)ˣ)
    {A B : (Fin 1 → ℂ) →L[ℂ] (Fin 1 → ℂ)} (hu : (u : V →L[ℂ] V) = A.prodMap B) :
    (((splitCoords 1 1).trans ((ContinuousLinearEquiv.unitsEquiv ℂ V u).trans
      (splitCoords 1 1).symm) : (Fin (1 + 1) → ℂ) ≃L[ℂ] (Fin (1 + 1) → ℂ)) :
        (Fin (1 + 1) → ℂ) →L[ℂ] (Fin (1 + 1) → ℂ)) =
      (splitCoords (𝕜 := ℂ) (M := ℂ) 1 1).symm.toContinuousLinearMap.comp
        ((A.prodMap B).comp (splitCoords (𝕜 := ℂ) (M := ℂ) 1 1).toContinuousLinearMap) := by
  ext1 v
  simp [ContinuousLinearEquiv.unitsEquiv_apply, hu]

end SymplecticGeometry.ProductSphere

/-! ### The clutched lines `L m` -/

namespace TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore

open SymplecticGeometry.ProductSphere

open scoped unitInterval

variable {X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X]

/-- The block coordinates of a point of the Whitney sum of two trivial lines depend continuously
on the point. -/
private theorem continuous_splitCoords_snd_whitneySum_trivial {B : Type*} [TopologicalSpace B] :
    Continuous fun p : (whitneySum (trivial ℂ B 1) (trivial ℂ B 1)).core.TotalSpace ↦
      splitCoords (𝕜 := ℂ) 1 1 p.snd := by
  obtain ⟨h₁, h₂⟩ := (continuous_mk_whitneySum_iff (trivial ℂ B 1) (trivial ℂ B 1)
    (b := fun p : (whitneySum (trivial ℂ B 1) (trivial ℂ B 1)).core.TotalSpace ↦ p.proj)
    (s := fun p ↦ p.snd)).1 continuous_id
  exact (continuous_trivial_iff.1 h₁).2.prodMk (continuous_trivial_iff.1 h₂).2

/-- Hatcher's rotation as an automorphism of the pullback of the sum of two trivial lines to
`(X × I) × Circle`, with fibre map `rotationHomotopy m n t u` at `((x, t), u)`. -/
private def rotationHomotopyIso (m n : ℤ) :
    ((whitneySum (trivial ℂ X 1) (trivial ℂ X 1)).pullback
        (ContinuousMap.fst : C(X × I, X))).pullback
        (ContinuousMap.fst : C((X × I) × Circle, X × I)) ≅
      ((whitneySum (trivial ℂ X 1) (trivial ℂ X 1)).pullback
        (ContinuousMap.fst : C(X × I, X))).pullback
        (ContinuousMap.fst : C((X × I) × Circle, X × I)) :=
  -- The pullback of the sum of two trivial lines is the sum of two trivial lines, by unfolding.
  isoOfContinuousEquiv (A := whitneySum (trivial ℂ ((X × I) × Circle) 1) (trivial ℂ _ 1))
    (D := whitneySum (trivial ℂ ((X × I) × Circle) 1) (trivial ℂ _ 1))
    (fun b ↦ (splitCoords 1 1).trans ((ContinuousLinearEquiv.unitsEquiv ℂ _
      (rotationHomotopy m n b.1.2 b.2)).trans (splitCoords 1 1).symm)) <| by
    have hb : Continuous fun p : (whitneySum (trivial ℂ ((X × I) × Circle) 1)
        (trivial ℂ ((X × I) × Circle) 1)).core.TotalSpace ↦ p.proj :=
      FiberBundle.continuous_proj _ _
    have hv := ((continuous_rotationHomotopy m n).comp
      ((continuous_snd.comp (continuous_fst.comp hb)).prodMk (continuous_snd.comp hb))).clm_apply
        continuous_splitCoords_snd_whitneySum_trivial
    refine (continuous_mk_whitneySum_iff _ _).2 ⟨continuous_trivial_iff.2 ⟨hb, ?_⟩,
      continuous_trivial_iff.2 ⟨hb, ?_⟩⟩
    · exact (continuous_fst.comp hv).congr fun p ↦
        congrArg Prod.fst ((splitCoords (𝕜 := ℂ) (M := ℂ) 1 1).apply_symm_apply _).symm
    · exact (continuous_snd.comp hv).congr fun p ↦
        congrArg Prod.snd ((splitCoords (𝕜 := ℂ) (M := ℂ) 1 1).apply_symm_apply _).symm

private theorem fiberMap_rotationHomotopyIso_zero (m n : ℤ) (w : X × Circle) :
    (rotationHomotopyIso (X := X) m n).hom.fiberMap ((w.1, 0), w.2) =
      (whitneyMapIso (circleZPowIso X m) (circleZPowIso X n)).hom.fiberMap w := by
  refine (fiberMap_isoOfContinuousEquiv_hom _ _ _).trans ?_
  rw [whitneyMapIso_hom, fiberMap_whitneyMap, fiberMap_circleZPowIso_hom,
    fiberMap_circleZPowIso_hom]
  exact splitCoords_conj_unitsEquiv _ (rotationHomotopy_zero m n w.2)

private theorem fiberMap_rotationHomotopyIso_one (m n : ℤ) (w : X × Circle) :
    (rotationHomotopyIso (X := X) m n).hom.fiberMap ((w.1, 1), w.2) =
      (whitneyMapIso (circleZPowIso X (m + n)) (circleZPowIso X 0)).hom.fiberMap w := by
  refine (fiberMap_isoOfContinuousEquiv_hom _ _ _).trans ?_
  rw [whitneyMapIso_hom, fiberMap_whitneyMap, fiberMap_circleZPowIso_hom,
    fiberMap_circleZPowIso_hom]
  exact splitCoords_conj_unitsEquiv _ (rotationHomotopy_one m n w.2)

/-- **The lines `L m` add up as their degrees.** Over a paracompact R₁ space `X`, for instance a
compact Hausdorff one, let `L m` be the line over `X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)` clutched from the trivial
line by `u ↦ u ^ m` (`circleZPowIso X m`). Then `L m ⊕ L n ≅ L (m + n) ⊕ L 0`. -/
theorem whitneySum_clutching_circleZPowIso [ParacompactSpace X] [R1Space X] (m n : ℤ) :
    Nonempty (whitneySum ((trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X m))
        ((trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X n)) ≅
      whitneySum ((trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X (m + n)))
        ((trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X 0))) := by
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_iso_clutching_of_homotopic
    (E := whitneySum (trivial ℂ X 1) (trivial ℂ X 1))
    (f₀ := whitneyMapIso (circleZPowIso X m) (circleZPowIso X n))
    (f₁ := whitneyMapIso (circleZPowIso X (m + n)) (circleZPowIso X 0))
    (rotationHomotopyIso m n) (fiberMap_rotationHomotopyIso_zero m n)
    (fiberMap_rotationHomotopyIso_one m n)
  exact ⟨(clutchingWhitneySumIso _ _).symm ≪≫ e ≪≫ clutchingWhitneySumIso _ _⟩

end TauCeti.FiniteRankBundleCore

/-! ### The classes of the lines `L m` in `K(X × ℂP¹)` -/

namespace TauCeti.SplitK0

open FiniteRankBundleCore

variable {X : Type} [TopologicalSpace X]

/-- The line `L 0`, clutched from the trivial line by the constant `1`, has the class `1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem of_clutching_circleZPowIso_zero :
    (of ((trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X 0)) :
      SplitK0 (FiniteRankBundleCore ℂ (X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)))) = 1 := by
  rw [circleZPowIso_zero, of_congr (clutchingOneIso _), one_def]
  exact of_congr (eqToIso (pullback_tensorUnit _))

/-- The line `L (-1)`, clutched from the trivial line by `u ↦ u⁻¹`, has the class `[H]` of the
pullback of the tautological line of `ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)`. -/
theorem of_clutching_circleZPowIso_neg_one :
    (of ((trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X (-1))) :
      SplitK0 (FiniteRankBundleCore ℂ (X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)))) =
      of ((Projectivization.tautologicalCore ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)).pullback ContinuousMap.snd) :=
  of_congr (clutchingZIso X)

variable [ParacompactSpace X] [R1Space X]

/-- **The class of `L m`.** Over a paracompact R₁ space `X`, the line over `X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)`
clutched from the trivial line by `u ↦ u ^ m` has the class `1 + m • (1 - [H])`, with `[H]` the
class of the pullback of the tautological line. -/
theorem of_clutching_circleZPowIso (m : ℤ) :
    (of ((trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X m)) :
      SplitK0 (FiniteRankBundleCore ℂ (X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)))) =
      1 + m • (1 - of ((Projectivization.tautologicalCore ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)).pullback
        ContinuousMap.snd)) := by
  have key (m n : ℤ) : (of ((trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X m)) :
      SplitK0 (FiniteRankBundleCore ℂ (X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)))) +
      of ((trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X n)) =
      of ((trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X (m + n))) + 1 := by
    obtain ⟨e⟩ := whitneySum_clutching_circleZPowIso (X := X) m n
    rw [← of_whitneySum, of_congr e, of_whitneySum, of_clutching_circleZPowIso_zero]
  have h₁ := key 1 (-1)
  rw [of_clutching_circleZPowIso_neg_one, show (1 : ℤ) + -1 = 0 by norm_num,
    of_clutching_circleZPowIso_zero] at h₁
  induction m using Int.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | succ k ih =>
    have h := key k 1
    rw [add_smul, one_smul]
    linear_combination (norm := abel) -h + ih + h₁
  | pred k ih =>
    have h := key (-(k : ℤ) - 1) 1
    rw [show -(k : ℤ) - 1 + 1 = -k by ring] at h
    rw [sub_smul, one_smul]
    linear_combination (norm := abel) h + ih - h₁

/-- **`[H⁻¹] = 2 - [H]`.** Over a paracompact R₁ space `X`, the line over `X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)`
clutched from the trivial line by `u ↦ u`, the inverse of the pullback `H` of the tautological
line, has the class `2 - [H]`. -/
theorem of_clutching_circleZPowIso_one :
    (of ((trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X 1)) :
      SplitK0 (FiniteRankBundleCore ℂ (X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)))) =
      2 - of ((Projectivization.tautologicalCore ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)).pullback ContinuousMap.snd) := by
  rw [of_clutching_circleZPowIso, one_smul, ← add_sub_assoc, one_add_one_eq_two]

/-- Over a paracompact R₁ space `X`, the class of every line `L m` clutched from the trivial line
by `u ↦ u ^ m` lies in the additive subgroup of `K(X × ℂP¹)` generated by `1` and `[H]`. -/
theorem of_clutching_circleZPowIso_mem_closure (m : ℤ) :
    (of ((trivial ℂ X 1).clutching (circleZPowIso X m)) :
      SplitK0 (FiniteRankBundleCore ℂ (X × ℙ ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)))) ∈
      AddSubgroup.closure {1,
        of ((Projectivization.tautologicalCore ℂ (Fin 2 → ℂ)).pullback ContinuousMap.snd)} := by
  rw [of_clutching_circleZPowIso]
  exact add_mem (AddSubgroup.subset_closure (by simp)) (zsmul_mem (sub_mem
    (AddSubgroup.subset_closure (by simp)) (AddSubgroup.subset_closure (by simp))) m)

end TauCeti.SplitK0

